### C-14 (MINOR → MAJOR) — MAJOR

`isProcessing` excludes the only phase that blocks the main thread. It is set inside runQuantize, AFTER `await imageFileToPixels(file)` — so createImageBitmap + drawImage + a 48MB getImageData, plus a second 48MB copy at `pixels.buffer.slice(0)`, all run on the main thread with the processing flag FALSE. The result: a half-second UI freeze during which the component's only accessible progress signal is provably absent. The module docstring advertising 'All run quantization off main thread with Transferable ArrayBuffer' is measurably false for the dominant cost.

- **Evidence:** useImageQuantize.ts:87 (flag set) vs :106 (the await it sits behind) · :18-26 imageFileToPixels · :93 `const buffer = pixels.buffer.slice(0)` · docstring :1-6. MEASURED (WBX-probe5.mjs, 4000x3000 PNG, 6,824,131 bytes): `wall ms (upload -> readout): 1077` · `longTasks: [517,63]  maxLongTask: 517  totalLongMs: 580` · `anySkeleton (isProcessing ever rendered): false` · the 60ms sampling interval stops firing from t=181ms to t=700ms — a 519ms hole that is the long task itself. Corroborated by WBX-probe2.mjs (`skeletons: 0` at 150/400/900/2000/4000/7000ms) and all four WBX-probe4.mjs snapshots.
- **Mechanism:** the async boundary is drawn in the wrong place — the worker offload offloads only the cheap part (k-means on <=10k sampled pixels) while two 48MB main-thread operations sit outside the state flag
- **Reproduction:** /#/extract → upload a 4000x3000 image. Main thread blocks 517ms; PaletteCardSkeleton (its role="status" aria-label="Loading palette" being the only accessible progress signal) never renders. Re-run: `node .../probe-r3/WBX-probe5.mjs`
- **Proposed cure:** createImageBitmap, OffscreenCanvas and getImageData are all available inside a worker. Post the File itself to quantize-worker.ts (File/Blob is structured-cloneable and cheap) and decode there. Main-thread pixel work drops to zero, the slice(0) copy disappears, decode failures arrive through the typed error channel that already exists, and isProcessing can honestly be set on the first synchronous line. One transposition folds C-5, C-7, C-14 and C-25.

### C-5 (extended) — BLOCKER

The corrupt-image failure is not merely silent — it is stale attribution. Run AFTER a successful extraction (the realistic sequence; r1 and r2 both reproduced only from a fresh pane), the workbench displays a broken <img> next to a k-rail gradient and a dominance readout that are byte-identical to the PREVIOUS image's, with no error line and an unhandled rejection. The preview is committed before anything decodes, and the fire-and-forget quantize call has no .catch.

- **Evidence:** useExtractSession.ts:164-168 (previewDataUrl written before decode) · :153-157 (runQuantize discards the promise, no .catch) · useImageQuantize.ts:105-108 → :18-26 (createImageBitmap unguarded). MEASURED (WBX-probe4.mjs, one session): `after-good : railBg="linear-gradient(to right, oklch(0.543346 0.174006 29.6967) 0%, …" code="oklch(54.334570875357% …29.696692379622deg)" destructiveLines=[] imgNaturalW=64` then `after-corrupt: railBg="…oklch(0.543346 0.174006 29.6967)…" (IDENTICAL) code="oklch(54.334570875357% …)" (IDENTICAL) destructiveLines=[] imgNaturalW=0 unhandled=["InvalidStateError: The source image could not be decoded."]` · `PAGEERRORS: ["InvalidStateError: The source image could not be decoded."]`. Screenshot: probe-r3/WBX-corrupt.png. Contradicts the component's own comments: ExtractWorkbench.vue:79 'error ≠ empty: an explicit destructive line' and ImageDropZone.vue:3 'the specimen never lies'.
- **Mechanism:** unguarded async with no error boundary; state committed ahead of validation, so a failure leaves a half-updated view that attributes old results to a new input
- **Reproduction:** /#/extract → upload a valid image (palette develops) → upload a file with mimeType image/png whose bytes are not a PNG. Broken preview + previous image's palette + zero error + one unhandledrejection + one pageerror. Recovers on the next valid upload (verified: after-recover shows a new gradient and readout). Re-run: `node .../probe-r3/WBX-probe4.mjs`
- **Proposed cure:** Decode first, commit second: one Result-returning intake pipeline where a decode failure sets quantizeError and leaves previewDataUrl and palette untouched. Falls out for free from the C-14 cure (decode in the worker, failure returns {type:'error', error:'image_decode_failed'} through the channel that already exists).

